            <ArticleTitle>Protracted epigastric pain and vomiting as a presentation of thyrotoxicosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>435-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Apathetic thyrotoxicosis is frequently difficult to recognize and can imitate a variety of diseases. A patient with a severe thyrotoxic state is reported, who presented with protracted epigastric pain and vomiting. Hyperthyroidism should be considered in patients with such prolonged and unexplained symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
